---
// biome-ignore lint/correctness/noUnusedImports: used in the template below; Biome's Astro frontmatter analysis doesn't see markup usage.
import { CalendarHeart, CircleQuestionMark, Heart } from "@lucide/astro";
// biome-ignore lint/correctness/noUnusedImports: used in the template below; Biome's Astro frontmatter analysis doesn't see markup usage.
import Button from "@/components/Button.astro";
// biome-ignore lint/correctness/noUnusedImports: used in the template below; Biome's Astro frontmatter analysis doesn't see markup usage.
import Card from "@/components/Card.astro";
// biome-ignore lint/correctness/noUnusedImports: used in the template below; Biome's Astro frontmatter analysis doesn't see markup usage.
import Divider from "@/components/Divider.astro";
// biome-ignore lint/correctness/noUnusedImports: used in the template below; Biome's Astro frontmatter analysis doesn't see markup usage.
import Hero from "@/components/Hero.astro";
// biome-ignore lint/correctness/noUnusedImports: used in the template below; Biome's Astro frontmatter analysis doesn't see markup usage.
import HouseSectionIcon from "@/components/HouseSectionIcon.astro";
// biome-ignore lint/correctness/noUnusedImports: used in the template below; Biome's Astro frontmatter analysis doesn't see markup usage.
import Section from "@/components/Section.astro";
// biome-ignore lint/correctness/noUnusedImports: used in the template below; Biome's Astro frontmatter analysis doesn't see markup usage.
import SectionHeader from "@/components/SectionHeader.astro";
// biome-ignore lint/correctness/noUnusedImports: used in the template below; Biome's Astro frontmatter analysis doesn't see markup usage.
import BaseLayout from "@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="Queen City Magic">
  <Hero />

  <Section width="wide">
    <div class="intro">
      <SectionHeader>
        <HouseSectionIcon slot="icon" />
        The magic explained&hellip;
      </SectionHeader>
      <p class="intro__aside">
        (to the best of our abilities&ndash;we are pleasantly surprised yearly ourselves)
      </p>
      <p class="intro__body">
        QCMM is a homegrown festival celebrating magic in all forms and from all fandoms. We
        love, accept and welcome kind humans from everywhere and every persuasion who come
        for fun, friends, a little mischief and a want to believe in the extra special parts
        of this existence — from great books to things you have to squint your eyes and
        concentrate to believe in. We are not affiliated with Warner Brothers or any other
        corporate entity. We are an army of volunteers who work year around to make sure that
        thousands of visitors to our town have the best hour or long weekend possible in our
        delightful, charming and downright magical historic downtown.
      </p>
    </div>

    <Divider />

    <Card>
      <CalendarHeart slot="icon" size={22} aria-hidden="true" />
      <h2 slot="title">Save the Date</h2>
      <p>
        Last year's crowd braved the wetness and turned it into one of our best festivals yet
        — thank you to every witch, wizard, and muggle who showed up and made the magic
        happen.
      </p>
      <p>
        Mark your calendars: Queen City Mischief &amp; Magic returns <strong
          >September 26&ndash;27, 2026</strong
        >, with more mischief, magic, mystery and mayhem than ever. We can't wait to see you
        there.
      </p>
      <Button slot="cta" href="/events">Plan Your Visit</Button>
    </Card>

    <Card>
      <Heart slot="icon" size={22} aria-hidden="true" />
      <h2 slot="title">You Belong Here</h2>
      <p>
        The people who work tirelessly on this festival for months do this as a hobby and
        labor of love. We update as we can and try to keep you as informed as possible but
        due to the nature of a FREE festival with a MILLION moving parts and things to do, it
        is hard to keep everyone abreast of everything. Just stay tuned, trust that when you
        arrive there will be way more things to do than you have time to do it and try to
        relax and ENJOY your time here&ndash;whether you do and see everything or do and see
        one thing. All you have to do is arrive and be wow-ed by a place and event that even
        those of us who live here and work on it can hardly believe exists. Staunton is
        magic! You will only be sorry if you miss it.
      </p>
      <Button slot="cta" href="/donate">Help Us Make the Magic</Button>
    </Card>

    <Card>
      <CircleQuestionMark slot="icon" size={22} aria-hidden="true" />
      <h2 slot="title">Learn more</h2>
      <p>
        The easiest way for us to update things is our <a
          href="https://www.facebook.com/queencitymagic"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          class="focus-glow">FB page</a
        >. Again, there are 100&ndash;200 people &amp; organizations involved. QCMM acts as
        the connector, cat-wranglers and communicator for all of this. There will be an FAQ,
        multiple maps and <a
          href="https://qcmm25.sched.com/"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          class="focus-glow">a scheduling app</a
        > FULL OF FUN released within a month of our start&ndash;and it will likely show up on
        FB first. We are set in a historic downtown so there is a roster of amazing small
        businesses who provide facilities, food and fun as well as a large group of local
        non-profits to paint faces, help with crafts and add to the event. We don't and can't
        allow vendors. We are grateful to our state tourism corporation for helping us with
        the task of welcoming 20,000+ visitors for QCMM.
      </p>
      <Button slot="cta" href="/faq">Read the FAQ</Button>
    </Card>
  </Section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  h2 {
    font-size: clamp(1.35rem, 3vw, 1.65rem);
    font-weight: 400;
    color: var(--color-surface-primary);
  }

  p {
    margin: 0;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .intro {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 1rem;
    max-width: 38rem;
    margin-inline: auto;
    text-align: center;
  }

  .intro__aside {
    font-style: italic;
    opacity: 0.8;
  }

  .intro__body {
    font-size: 1.2rem;
  }
</style>
